post.description:
Send the session token as `X-Wallet-Session: {sessionToken}`. The gateway strips `Authorization`. The signature covers exactly:

```
Cosmos Pay Wallet sign-in
email: {lowercased email}
account: {address}
at: {signedAt}
```

signed over those raw UTF-8 bytes with the account key, base64. The first line is one no Stellar transaction envelope can begin with, which is what makes signing it safe.

On Solana and Monad (`chain`), a `chain: {chain}` line follows the first one. Solana signs the bytes with ed25519 (`signMessage`; base64 or base58); Monad with EIP-191 `personal_sign` (0x-hex).

Requires the `payments:write` scope. The shared public key may call it.

put.description:
What `changePassword` on the device sends. No session: the signature is the credential, and it covers the SHA-256 of the box, so one signature stores exactly one box and cannot be replayed to store another. The bytes are:

```
Cosmos Pay Wallet backup
account: {address}
box: {sha256 hex of box}
at: {signedAt}
```

On Solana and Monad a `chain: {chain}` line follows the first one, and the bytes are signed as for sign-in.

Requires the `payments:write` scope. The shared public key may call it.

post.description:
Send the session token as `X-Wallet-Session: {sessionToken}`. The gateway strips `Authorization`. The signature covers exactly:

```
Cosmos Pay Wallet recovery setup
account: {stellarAddress}
signers: {signerA},{signerB}
at: {signedAt}
```

The envelope comes back signed by the sponsor only. Once per account: refused when the account already has a signer besides its master key.

Requires the `payments:write` scope. The shared public key may call it.
